{"duration_api_ms":95680,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0204548c-a824-57b7-bea3-1783011bc81a","total_cost_usd":0.7612170000000003,"usage":{"input_tokens":44,"cache_creation_input_tokens":37864,"cache_read_input_tokens":1296545,"output_tokens":9941,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1032},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":37864,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1255,"cache_read_input_tokens":69535,"cache_creation_input_tokens":583,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":583},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":44,"outputTokens":9941,"cacheReadInputTokens":1296545,"cacheCreationInputTokens":37864,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.7612170000000003,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1032,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":37864,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":22,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I measured a real speedup for small PDF exports and recorded it, but it's about 0.1 s per export, well below the plan's 0.3–0.6 s estimate. Both acceptance commands pass (`.theseus/oracle/unit.sh`: 178 passed, 1 skipped; `npm run lint:check`: exit 0 with one warning), and the work is committed on this branch.\n\n**What the change is.** `external/core` is still read-only, so I didn't write a code patch. It turned out none is needed for this cut: the installed x2t already loads V8 startup snapshots (pre-built copies of the editors' JavaScript engine state) from `sdkjs/<editor>/sdk-all.bin`, and `x2t -create-js-snapshots` creates them. The 9.3.7-1 package doesn't ship these files. The copies on this VM were left by an earlier attempt at this packet.\n\n**Proof of speed.** I ran `convert-large.js` 5 times per file on the three empty test documents, once with the snapshot files and once with them moved aside (restored afterwards). Median times for conversion to PDF through the server:\n\n| File | Without snapshots | With snapshots | Change |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| new.docx | 719 ms | 631 ms | −88 ms (−12%) |\n| new.xlsx | 722 ms | 621 ms | −101 ms (−14%) |\n| new.pptx | 1015 ms | 909 ms | −106 ms (−10%) |\n\nConversions that don't run the JavaScript engine were unchanged. Each setting was measured once, so treat about ±30 ms as noise.\n\n**Proof of equality.** P2's corpus oracle (`corpus.py`), run with the snapshots in place, gives `equal` against `baseline-9.3.7-1.json`.\n\n**Decisions:**\n- The fix belongs in installation, not in x2t: every install and upgrade should create the snapshot files, owned by user `ds`, and rebuild them when x2t or the scripts change. I didn't make that change, because it lives outside this packet's target. I requested it as a follow-up in `.theseus/spawn/PKT-0065-ship-v8-js-startup-snapshots-*.md`, which needs `documentserver`.\n- I set aside the other two candidates. Skipping `CDocBuilder::Initialize` would save too little: process start plus engine setup is only about 60 ms. Keeping a converter running between jobs is the only way to remove the rest of the fixed cost, but it needs a fork of `core` and its own diagnosis. I haven't requested it yet.\n- I dropped the earlier attempt's patch, whose hunk header the review flagged as wrong, because it isn't needed.\n\n**Surprises:**\n- The unit oracle failed once in `docsCoServerCrashPaths` (handshake auth tests), then passed three full runs in a row. It's flaky and probably caused attempt 2's acceptance failure. That file is outside the target, so I left it alone.\n- The repository had no record that an earlier attempt had created files on the VM.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas** (also written in the packet):\n- x2t uses `sdk-all.bin` snapshots when they're present, and the package doesn't ship them.\n- For small PDF exports, the remaining fixed cost (about 0.3–0.6 s) is the JavaScript warming up during the first conversion step, not starting the process or the engine.\n\nThe decision note is `.theseus/diagnosis/PKT-0065-x2t-js-snapshots.md`, next to the raw measurements (`PKT-0065-convert-large-*.json`). The Executor log and my friction line are filled in.","ttft_ms":2153,"type":"result","duration_ms":202231,"uuid":"67f7b8a9-7606-4f97-87ac-d0fda3c4bee6","ttft_stream_ms":1112,"time_to_request_ms":355,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":6,"system_prompt":203,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":17,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":32,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":14,"query_setup":5,"auto_mode_context_wait":9,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":31,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":3,"request_build":11},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":72,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":189,"time_to_request_major_faults":3,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":216,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":141,"process_rss_mib_result":235,"process_anon_mib_result":143,"process_peak_rss_mib":262,"process_cpu_ms_turn":4078,"process_wall_ms_turn":202230,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":1389,"process_wall_ms_streaming":80393,"main_stream_count":22,"main